# GitHub issue on "new ticket"

When the user opens work with **"New ticket"** (or similar) **for this repo**, create a **GitHub** issue on `earthboundtrev/integral` **before** writing code (or before starting Architect-skip backfill).

## Required first step

1. Parse the request into title + body (Summary, user story, acceptance criteria, definition of done).
2. Search open issues first (`gh issue list` / search) so duplicates are not created.
3. Create the issue:

```powershell
gh issue create --repo earthboundtrev/integral --title "..." --body "..." --label "enhancement"
```

Use label `bug` for defects, `enhancement` for features (create labels if missing, or omit if the repo has none).
4. Share the issue number/URL with the user immediately.
5. Use `#N` in branch names, commits, and PR bodies (`Closes #N`).

## Do not skip

- Do **not** rely on chat-only tracking for "new ticket" work.
- Spec/ADR gate still applies for new user-facing features (ADR-007 / `.cursor/rules/spec-driven-workflow.mdc`) after the issue exists.
- Other repos (e.g. Ducking Gravity, SmartAstro/astro) have their own new-ticket rules — this rule is for **Integral** only.

## When closing

- PR body must include `Closes #N`.
- After human merge (or clean backfill sign-off): **verify** `gh issue view {N} --json state` is `CLOSED`; close manually if needed (`scripts/post_merge_hygiene.ps1`).
- Delete the local ticket branch after merge.
